          "label": "JPL Horizons",
          "checked": "2026-09-21",
          "locator": "Satellite solution tnosat_v001_20136199_jpl",
          "quote": "(136199) Eris I Dysnomia # obs: 19 (2005-2018); Position uncertainty wrt primary on 2025-Jan-1: 110 km"
        },
        {
          "catalogueId": "doi-10-3847-psj-ace52a",
          "url": "https://doi.org/10.3847/PSJ/ace52a",
          "label": "Brown and Butler (2023), The Planetary Science Journal 4, 193; ALMA Band 6 and Band 7 thermal detection of Dysnomia",
          "checked": "2026-09-21"
        }
      ]
    },
    "haumea": {
      "text": "Haumea has two moons, Hiʻiaka and Namaka, and a ring. Hiʻiaka is the larger moon.",
